      "start": 0.77,
      "end": 2.45,
      "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.77,
      "end": 16.35,
      "text": "Glare usually comes from light hitting the paper straight on. Are they framed under glass?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.89,
      "end": 27.89,
      "text": "Take those out of the frames if you can. For all of them, put two lamps at forty five degrees on either side, and the camera dead centre."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.06,
      "end": 37.96,
      "text": "The lens pointing straight at the middle of the painting, parallel to it. If you tilt even slightly, the edges stop looking square."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 42.32,
      "end": 49.18,
      "text": "Put a grey card or a white sheet in the first shot and set white balance from that. Then compare the photo to the real painting next to the screen."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 53.68,
      "end": 57.86,
      "text": "It's worth it for a gallery. The jury only sees the photo, never the original."
